          %p
            An obvious question is: does this process ever terminate? In unpublished work of Lack, it is
            %a{:href => "#Taylor"} claimed
            that this process terminates at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_3
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 3
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{T_3} \dashv u_{T_3}
            is a nuclear adjunction. Thus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 5
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_3 \simeq T_5 \simeq \dots
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 6
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_4 \simeq D_6 \simeq \dots
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℓ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+complete"} Cauchy complete
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_2
          %p
            Under the simplifying assumptions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completeness"} Cauchy completeness
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PavlovicHughes20"} Pavlovic–Hughes
            %span.newWikiWord
              pseudo-idempotent 2-monad
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pseudo-idempotent+2-monad"} ?
            on a 2-category of monads in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            Note that this construction is distinct from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+decomposition"} monadic decomposition
